The model takes a 256x256 RGB image and returns four corner heatmaps and a
page mask. Everything SnapIQ does with that output - choosing the quarter
turn, fitting the page's edges, walking out to where the sheet ends, the
gradient check, and the straightening and cleaning that follow - is SnapIQ's
own work.
